2:Tf37,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-ai-tools-turn-images-into-painting#article","headline":"Best AI tools to turn images into a painting","description":"Which AI tool turns a photo into a painting? Five compared on style control, whether the subject survives, and repeating a look across many images.","url":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-ai-tools-turn-images-into-painting","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-ai-tools-turn-images-into-painting"},"datePublished":"2026-09-02","dateModified":"2026-09-02","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Melius Team","url":"https://www.melius.com"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://www.melius.com/#organization"},"isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.melius.com/#website"},"inLanguage":"en-US","image":"https://www.melius.com/images/blog/best-ai-tools-turn-images-into-painting/cover.webp","timeRequired":"PT9M","wordCount":1645,"articleSection":"Comparisons","keywords":"Comparisons"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Blog","item":"https://www.melius.com/blog"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Best AI tools to turn images into a painting","item":"https://www.melius.com/blog/best-ai-tools-turn-images-into-painting"}]},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the best AI tool to turn an image into a painting?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For one image, a preset tool is the right call, and of the five here Krea's preset library is the widest. For a painterly look you'll reuse across many images, Melius, because the style becomes an editable written description you reapply. NightCafe is the fastest way to test the idea, since it runs without a login and gives five free creations a day."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a free way to turn a photo into a painting?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. NightCafe gives up to five free creations a day with no login at all, Krea offers 100 daily compute units free with no credit card, and ComfyUI is free and open source if you'll run it yourself. Free output is usually lower resolution and daily caps apply, so read the terms if the image is going anywhere public."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I keep the subject recognizable?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Start with the effect low and increase it, and use a sharp, well-lit source. Faces and text distort first, so if either has to survive, name it in the instruction as something that must not change. On a canvas you can also branch and compare a subtle version against a heavy one before deciding."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use an AI painting of my photo commercially?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It varies by tool, so check first, and the free consumer converters are the ones most likely to restrict it. On Melius you own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I copy a specific artist's style?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often technically, and it carries real legal and ethical exposure, most of all for living artists and commercial work. Describe the technique, the palette, and the era, without naming a person. That avoids the problem and tends to produce something more distinctive anyway."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why do my painterly images look inconsistent?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Because a preset gets applied per image with no fixed reference behind it, so small differences between your source photos surface as visibly different results. Fix it by holding the style constant outside the tool: write the palette, lighting, and brushwork down once, or train a style, and apply that same thing to every image."}}]}]}7:X
