14:["$","p","b2380",{"children":["The other thing to watch is how much of your original survives. A painterly pass that loses your subject's face, or your product's shape, hasn't done the job, and tools differ on that more than on how attractive the output looks."]}]
15:["$","h2","b2382",{"id":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What to know before you pick"]}]
16:["$","ul","b2384-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b2384",{"children":["One image or a set? Presets win one-offs, described styles win consistency"]}],["$","li","b2386",{"children":["Faces, legible text, and product shapes break down first under a heavy painterly pass"]}],["$","li","b2388",{"children":["A style captured as text is reusable months later. A preset click isn't."]}],["$","li","b2390",{"children":["Commercial rights differ per tool, so check before anything goes out publicly"]}]]}]
17:["$","h2","b2392",{"id":"what-separates-a-good-photo-to-painting-tool","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What separates a good photo-to-painting tool?"]}]
18:["$","p","b2394",{"children":["Four things worth testing before you commit."]}]
19:["$","h3","b2396",{"children":["Style specificity"]}]
1a:["$","p","b2398",{"children":["There's a wide gap between picking oil painting from a menu and specifying warm golden-hour light from camera-left with painterly bokeh and a terracotta palette. The second is what you need to match an existing look."]}]
1b:["$","h3","b2400",{"children":["Subject survival"]}]
1c:["$","p","b2402",{"children":["The painterly effect and the recognizable subject pull against each other. Turn the effect up and the face goes; turn it down and it reads as a filter. A good tool lets you sit between those, and lets you say what must not change."]}]
1d:["$","h3","b2404",{"children":["Repeatability"]}]
1e:["$","p","b2406",{"children":["If image two has to match image one, the style needs to live outside the session as a saved reference, a written description, or a trained model. Otherwise small differences in your source photos produce visibly different results."]}]
1f:["$","h3","b2408",{"children":["Rights you can act on"]}]
20:["$","p","b2410",{"children":["Free consumer tools and professional platforms answer the commercial-use question differently, and copying a living artist's style raises real exposure on top of that. Know where you stand before you publish."]}]
21:["$","h2","b2412",{"id":"the-five-compared","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["The five compared"]}]
22:["$","div","b2413",{"role":"region","aria-label":"Comparison table, scroll horizontally to see all columns","tabIndex":0,"data-lenis-prevent":true,"className":"my-10 max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-white shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-orange","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-left","children":["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","b2414",{"className":"bg-black/[0.04]","children":[["$","td","b24140",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b2417",{"children":[["$","strong","b2416",{"children":[""]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b24141",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b2420",{"children":[["$","strong","b2419",{"children":["How you specify a style"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b24142",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b2423",{"children":[["$","strong","b2422",{"children":["Repeatable across a set"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b24143",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b2426",{"children":[["$","strong","b2425",{"children":["Editing after the pass"]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b2427",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b24270",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2430",{"children":["Melius"]}]]}],["$","td","b24271",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2433",{"children":["Template, or a written style description from references"]}]]}],["$","td","b24272",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2436",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b24273",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2439",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b2440",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b24400",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2443",{"children":["Krea"]}]]}],["$","td","b24401",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2446",{"children":["1000+ preset styles, style transfer, trained LoRA"]}]]}],["$","td","b24402",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2449",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b24403",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2452",{"children":["4/5"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b2453",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b24530",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2456",{"children":["ComfyUI"]}]]}],["$","td","b24531",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2459",{"children":["You wire the pipeline yourself"]}]]}],["$","td","b24532",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2462",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b24533",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2465",{"children":["4/5"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b2466",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b24660",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2469",{"children":["NightCafe"]}]]}],["$","td","b24661",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2472",{"children":["Named preset styles"]}]]}],["$","td","b24662",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b2475",{"children":["4/5"]}]]}],"$L5a"]}],"$L5b"]}]}]}]
23:["$","h2","b2493",{"id":"1-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["1. Melius"]}]
24:["$","p","b2495",{"children":["Melius is a node-based creative canvas that empowers creators with AI agents to drive their work. It's first here because it covers both halves of the choice above: there's a one-click route, and there's a route that makes the look repeatable."]}]
25:["$","p","b2497",{"children":["The quick way is the Painting Transformation template, which turns a photo into an oil or watercolor painting. The controllable way is the Image Style Analysis template: you drop two to ten reference images on the canvas, group them, and the template reads the group and writes out a description covering palette, lighting, mood, composition, and depth of field."]}]
26:["$","h3","b2499",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
27:["$","ul","b2501-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b2501",{"children":["Gives you a preset and an editable style description, so a one-off and a campaign use the same tool"]}],["$","li","b2503",{"children":["The style description is plain text you can rewrite where it's wrong, then paste into another canvas next month"]}],["$","li","b2507",{"children":[["$","$L5c","b2505",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b2504","href":"/blog/nano-banana-image-models","isNewTab":false},"children":["Nano Banana Pro"]}]," holds to a detailed style brief closely, which is what makes a described look land"]}],["$","li","b2509",{"children":["Every re-run saves as a new version on the node, so a warmer take and a cooler one sit side by side, with neither overwritten"]}],["$","li","b2511",{"children":["Adjacent templates cover neighboring styles: Comic Book Style, Pixel Art, Media-to-Anime, Sketch to Image, and Film Camera"]}]]}]
28:["$","p","b2513",{"children":["The qualifier is that the described-style route asks for setup you may not want. If you have one photo and want it painted this afternoon, running a style analysis first is more machinery than the job needs, and a phone app will get you there faster."]}]
29:["$","p","b2518",{"children":["You own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms, and Melius does not use your work to train AI models. Every model runs from ",["$","$L5c","b2516",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b2515","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false},"children":["one subscription"]}]," across the library of leading models."]}]
2a:["$","p","b2524",{"children":[["$","strong","b2519",{"children":["Best for: "]}],"a painterly look applied consistently across a set, and brand or campaign work where the style has to be defensible next quarter. ",["$","$L5c","b2522",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b2521","href":"/pricing","isNewTab":false},"children":["See pricing"]}]," for plans and credits."]}]
2b:["$","h2","b2526",{"id":"2-krea","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["2. Krea"]}]
2c:["$","p","b2528",{"children":["Krea is a strong specialist on this list and the closest competitor on repeatability. It offers over 1000 preset styles alongside genuine style transfer, and it lets you train a custom model on your own images through LoRA fine-tuning, which is the most literal form of a reusable style available anywhere here."]}]
2d:["$","h3","b2530",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
2e:["$","ul","b2532-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b2532",{"children":["Over 1000 preset styles, so the odds of finding your look without describing it are high"]}],["$","li","b2534",{"children":["Custom style training via LoRA on faces, products, or styles, available in limited form even on the free plan"]}],["$","li","b2536",{"children":["Upscaling to 22K across seven different models, useful when a painterly pass softens detail"]}],["$","li","b2538",{"children":["Real-time generation in under 50 milliseconds, which turns style-hunting into something you do by feel"]}],["$","li","b2540",{"children":["A free tier with 100 daily compute units and no credit card"]}]]}]
2f:["$","p","b2542",{"children":["Training a style is more commitment than writing one down, and it's less legible afterwards: a trained model is a black box where a written description is something a teammate can read and edit. Krea is also a suite of many capabilities, so painting is one thing it does among generation, video, 3D, and enhancement, which cuts both ways depending on whether you want focus or coverage."]}]
30:["$","p","b2545",{"children":[["$","strong","b2543",{"children":["Best for: "]}],"anyone who wants a trained, reusable style and the widest preset library of the five to start from."]}]
31:["$","h2","b2547",{"id":"3-comfyui","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["3. ComfyUI"]}]
32:["$","p","b2549",{"children":["ComfyUI is the honest answer for anyone who wants total control and is willing to pay for it in time. It's an open-source node-based interface where you wire the pipeline yourself, which means any style-transfer approach that exists can be built in it, at whatever precision you want."]}]
33:["$","h3","b2551",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
34:["$","ul","b2553-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b2553",{"children":["Complete control over every stage of the pipeline"]}],["$","li","b2555",{"children":["Free and open source, with Comfy Desktop for self-hosting and a managed Comfy Cloud that has a free tier to start on"]}],["$","li","b2557",{"children":["The graph is the record, so a working style pipeline is exactly reproducible"]}],["$","li","b2559",{"children":["A community-built ecosystem of more than 60,000 nodes and thousands of shareable workflows"]}]]}]
35:["$","p","b2561",{"children":["The cost is that you have to learn it, and nobody is coming to help. Setup, model management, and debugging are yours."]}]
36:["$","p","b2563",{"children":["An App Mode exists to simplify the interface for beginners, though the full node graph is the reason to choose it. It's the right tool if the pipeline is the point and the wrong one if the painting is."]}]
37:["$","p","b2566",{"children":[["$","strong","b2564",{"children":["Best for: "]}],"technical users who want to own the pipeline and don't mind maintaining it."]}]
38:["$","h2","b2568",{"id":"4-nightcafe","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["4. NightCafe"]}]
39:["$","p","b2570",{"children":["NightCafe is the lowest-friction way to find out whether this idea works for your photo at all. Its photo-to-painting page runs without a login and gives up to five free creations a day."]}]
3a:["$","p","b2572",{"children":["The styles are the ones people actually ask for: oil painting, watercolor, impressionist brushwork, pencil sketch, and more graphic digital looks."]}]
3b:["$","h3","b2574",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
3c:["$","ul","b2576-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b2576",{"children":["No login and no card to try it, which removes every reason not to test your own image first"]}],["$","li","b2578",{"children":["Five free creations a day, enough to compare a few styles on the same photo"]}],["$","li","b2580",{"children":["The classic painterly styles covered directly and named"]}],["$","li","b2582",{"children":["A community around it, useful for seeing what a style does before you commit your own picture to it"]}]]}]
3d:["$","p","b2584",{"children":["The limit is control. You're choosing from styles instead of specifying one, so matching an exact reference is not what it's for, and paid plans buy more credits and models rather than more precision."]}]
3e:["$","p","b2587",{"children":[["$","strong","b2585",{"children":["Best for: "]}],"trying the idea at no cost, and one-off personal images where a good-looking result matters more than an exact style."]}]
3f:["$","h2","b2589",{"id":"5-artguru","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["5. Artguru"]}]
40:["$","p","b2591",{"children":["Artguru goes narrower on one thing: making the output look like an actual painting instead of a filtered photograph. You upload a photo, pick a style, and it handles the rest."]}]
41:["$","p","b2593",{"children":["It publishes over ten art styles, with oil painting and watercolor alongside sketch, cartoon, concept art, and cyberpunk, and it says the set keeps growing."]}]
42:["$","h3","b2595",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
43:["$","ul","b2597-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b2597",{"children":["Oil painting and watercolor treated as the headline jobs, not as two entries in a long list"]}],["$","li","b2599",{"children":["Over ten styles, broad enough to cover illustrative looks as well as painterly ones"]}],["$","li","b2601",{"children":["A three-step flow with nothing to configure, so there's no setup between you and a result"]}]]}]
44:["$","p","b2603",{"children":["It's a focused tool, so there's no wider editor and no workflow around it, and its own page doesn't state pricing or free-tier limits, so check those before you rely on it for anything commercial."]}]
45:["$","p","b2606",{"children":[["$","strong","b2604",{"children":["Best for: "]}],"convincing painterly texture on a single image, when you want a named style and no decisions."]}]
46:["$","h2","b2608",{"id":"turning-a-reference-into-a-direction-on-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Turning a reference into a direction on Melius"]}]
47:["$","p","b2610",{"children":["Drop the reference on the canvas and run Image Style Analysis on it. That turns somebody's mood board into a written direction, which is the thing that survives the handoff: an approved image can only be copied, but a described style can be argued with, edited and reapplied months later."]}]
48:["$","p","b2612",{"children":["Branch from there rather than iterating in place. Five directions become five branches off one reference, sitting side by side where you can actually compare them, and the one that gets approved is already a working configuration you point at the next asset. Sketch to Image resolves a rough drawing if you're starting from paper, and the brand anchor keeps concepts inside the brand instead of drifting out of it."]}]
49:["$","p","b2614",{"children":["For the loosest, strangest end of exploration, a dedicated image model will still propose more than this will. Use one, then bring the direction back here to make it repeatable."]}]
4a:["$","p","b2619",{"children":["If the painterly pass is one step inside a larger image job, the neighboring question is what happens behind the subject: see ",["$","$L5c","b2617",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b2616","href":"/blog/best-ai-photo-background-editing-tools","isNewTab":false},"children":["the best AI photo background editing tools"]}],"."]}]
4b:["$","p","b2624",{"children":["Start from the Painting Transformation template, then capture what worked as a style you can reuse. ",["$","$L5c","b2622",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b2621","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true},"children":["Open Melius"]}],"."]}]
4c:["$","h2","b2626",{"id":"frequently-asked-questions","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Frequently asked questions"]}]
4d:["$","div","b2627",{"className":"faq-list my-10 flex flex-col divide-y divide-black/10 border-y border-black/10","children":[["$","details","0",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is the best AI tool to turn an image into a painting?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"For one image, a preset tool is the right call, and of the five here Krea's preset library is the widest. For a painterly look you'll reuse across many images, Melius, because the style becomes an editable written description you reapply. NightCafe is the fastest way to test the idea, since it runs without a login and gives five free creations a day."}]]}],["$","details","1",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Is there a free way to turn a photo into a painting?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes. NightCafe gives up to five free creations a day with no login at all, Krea offers 100 daily compute units free with no credit card, and ComfyUI is free and open source if you'll run it yourself. Free output is usually lower resolution and daily caps apply, so read the terms if the image is going anywhere public."}]]}],["$","details","2",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["How do I keep the subject recognizable?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Start with the effect low and increase it, and use a sharp, well-lit source. Faces and text distort first, so if either has to survive, name it in the instruction as something that must not change. On a canvas you can also branch and compare a subtle version against a heavy one before deciding."}]]}],["$","details","3",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can I use an AI painting of my photo commercially?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":"$L5d"}]]}],"$L5e"]}],"$L5f","$L60"]}]
4e:["$","section","related",{"className":"relative w-full pb-section bg-gray-background","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"color":"gray"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-300 px-5 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-h-2 mb-12 text-center text-balance text-gray-dark-1","children":"Related Articles"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto grid w-full max-w-max grid-cols-1 gap-11 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","$L61","post-best-ai-tools-product-photo-variants",{"post":{"_key":"post-best-ai-tools-product-photo-variants","slug":"best-ai-tools-product-photo-variants","category":"comparisons","title":"Best AI tools for producing product photo variants","isoDate":"2026-09-01","date":"September 1, 2026","readTime":"9 Min Read","excerpt":"Which AI tool should you use for product photo variants? Five tools compared on product fidelity, batch output and channel resizing, with the trade-offs.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/best-ai-tools-product-photo-variants/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the best AI tool for product photo variants?","answer":"For teams producing variants across many SKUs, Melius, because it anchors every generation on your pack shot, your real product page specs and your logo as separate inputs, then resizes on the same canvas. If your variants are paid social ads, Cuttable closes the publish-and-measure loop and Creatify does the same for video. Flair is the pick if product and on-model imagery is the whole job, and Pencil if procurement requirements decide your tooling."},{"question":"How do I stop AI from changing my product?","answer":"Give it three inputs, not one. Upload a clean pack shot rather than a lifestyle photo, so the model can see the product itself. Supply your product page specs so it has real dimensions and materials. Add your logo as its own reference with an instruction not to redraw it. Proportion drift is usually caused by missing inputs, not by weak prompting."},{"question":"Can AI keep packaging text legible?","answer":"Yes, but the model decides it. Typography and material fidelity are won by different image models, so pick per job: a style-adherent model for lifestyle and material shots, a typography-strong one when the label has to read. Running both from one subscription is what makes comparing them cheap."},{"question":"How many variants should I generate per run?","answer":"Three or four. Image models are probabilistic, so running several in parallel beats running one, disliking it and starting over. Correct the near-misses by editing that step's prompt rather than rewriting the whole brief."},{"question":"Do I still need a photographer for product photos?","answer":"For most catalog and lifestyle variants, no, but you do need one clean, well-lit pack shot per product, and everything else is generated from it, so that shot is worth paying for. Reflective and transparent products and print-resolution hero images still favor a real shoot and manual retouching."},{"question":"Is an ad platform or a canvas the right choice for product variants?","answer":"Ask where the output goes. If it goes straight into Meta or TikTok as a tested ad, an ad production system saves you the handoff. If it goes into a catalog, a marketplace listing, a deck or a packaging render, a canvas is the better shape, because those destinations need control more than they need automatic publishing."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"which-ai-tool-should-you-use-for-product-photo-variants","title":"Which tool"},{"_key":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","title":"Before you pick"},{"_key":"what-separates-a-good-product-variant-tool","title":"What separates them"},{"_key":"the-five-compared","title":"The five compared"},{"_key":"1-melius","title":"1. Melius"},{"_key":"2-flair","title":"2. Flair"},{"_key":"3-cuttable","title":"3. Cuttable"},{"_key":"4-pencil","title":"4. Pencil"},{"_key":"5-creatify","title":"5. Creatify"},{"_key":"what-a-variant-set-actually-costs-you","title":"What it costs"},{"_key":"producing-variants-on-melius","title":"Producing on Melius"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2055","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2054","text":"Which AI tool should you use for product photo variants?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"which-ai-tool-should-you-use-for-product-photo-variants"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2057","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2056","text":"Pick the tool that holds your actual product steady across every variant, because that's the part that decides whether a batch ships or gets redone by hand. Generating one good-looking shot is solved. Generating forty where the proportions, the material and the logo are still right in all forty isn't.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2059","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2058","text":"The tools below split into two shapes. Some are ad-production systems that take your product and fire out finished creative for Meta and TikTok. Others are canvases where you build the shot yourself and keep control of every step. Neither is better in the abstract, and the mismatch between them is usually why a tool disappoints.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2061","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2060","text":"What to know before you pick","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-to-know-before-you-pick"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2063","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2062","text":"Input fidelity beats output quality. A beautiful product shot is worthless if the product in it isn't quite yours.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2065","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2064","text":"Feed the model your real specs. Dimensions, materials and color codes from your product detail page fix proportion drift that prompting won't.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2067","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2066","text":"Material fidelity and legible packaging text are won by different image models, so split the work across two models","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2069","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2068","text":"A variant set isn't finished until it exists in every aspect ratio you ship, so weigh the resizing step as heavily as the generating step","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2071","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2070","text":"What separates a good product variant tool?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-separates-a-good-product-variant-tool"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2073","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2072","text":"Four things, in rough order of how often they're the reason a tool gets abandoned.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2075","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2074","text":"It keeps your product yours","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2077","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2076","text":"The failure everyone hits is a product that's almost right. Proportions drift, a logo gets redrawn as a similar-looking shape, fabric drapes generically. A good tool takes your pack shot, your logo file and your real dimensions as separate inputs and holds all three.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2079","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2078","text":"It produces sets, not shots","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2081","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2080","text":"One hero image is a demo. The job is a SKU across five scenes, or one winning ad across fifty variants. Look at what happens on the second product, not the first.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2083","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2082","text":"It handles text on packaging","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2085","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2084","text":"Labels, product names and packaging copy are where generative passes fall apart fastest. If your product has visible type, test that before anything else, because a tool that can't render it legibly can't do your job at all.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2087","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2086","text":"It finishes the job","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2089","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2088","text":"Variants need to exist at 1x1, 4x5, 9x16 and more. A tool that generates beautifully and leaves you cropping by hand has moved the bottleneck rather than removing it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2091","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2090","text":"The five compared","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-five-compared"},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b2092","rows":[{"_key":"b2093","cells":[{"_key":"b2094","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2096","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2095","text":"","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2097","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2099","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2098","text":"Shape","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2100","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2102","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2101","text":"Product fidelity inputs","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2103","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2105","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2104","text":"Batch","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2106","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2108","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2107","text":"Resizing","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2109","cells":[{"_key":"b2110","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2112","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2111","text":"Melius","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2113","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2115","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2114","text":"Agent-run node canvas","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2116","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2118","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2117","text":"Pack shot, product page specs, logo node","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2119","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2121","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2120","text":"Canvas duplication and upload swap","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2122","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2124","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2123","text":"Magic Resize, re-composes per ratio","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2125","cells":[{"_key":"b2126","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2128","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2127","text":"Flair","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2129","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2131","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2130","text":"Drag-and-drop staging canvas","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2132","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2134","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2133","text":"Pack shot, props, on-model","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2135","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2137","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2136","text":"Yes","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2138","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2140","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2139","text":"Not a headline feature","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2141","cells":[{"_key":"b2142","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2144","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2143","text":"Cuttable","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2145","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2147","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2146","text":"Ad production system","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2148","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2150","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2149","text":"Brand-trained on your assets","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2151","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2153","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2152","text":"Yes, batch ad generation","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2154","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2156","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2155","text":"Automatic on publish","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2157","cells":[{"_key":"b2158","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2160","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2159","text":"Pencil","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2161","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2163","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2162","text":"Enterprise creative platform","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2164","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2166","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2165","text":"Brand assets under governance","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2167","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2169","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2168","text":"Yes, across 24 markets","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2170","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2172","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2171","text":"Not stated","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2173","cells":[{"_key":"b2174","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2176","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2175","text":"Creatify","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2177","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2179","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2178","text":"Video-first ad platform","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2180","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2182","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2181","text":"Product Ads, URL-to-video","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2183","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2185","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2184","text":"Up to 50 video variants","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2186","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2188","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2187","text":"Per-network formats","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2190","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2189","text":"1. Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"1-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2192","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2191","text":"Melius is an agentic platform for creative work: a node-based creative canvas that AI agents drive. Each prompt, uploaded image and result is a node, and edges pass one node's output into the next, so a variant pipeline sits in front of you as a graph you can rewire.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2194","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2193","text":"For product work, the fidelity story is the reason to use it. You drop your pack shot on as a file node, and if you've got several angles you group them so the agent references all of them.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2196","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2195","text":"Paste the product page URL into the chat and Mel, the Melius agent, scrapes it into a text node holding your real dimensions, materials and color codes. Your logo goes on as its own node with an instruction not to redraw it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2198","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2197","text":"Those three inputs do the work. The failure mode that comes without them: given only a single photo, the model has to guess at the proportions.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2200","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2199","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2202","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2201","text":"Splits models by job. Nano Banana Pro carries material, fabric, food and editorial lighting; GPT Image 2 renders type that stays legible on packaging.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2204","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2203","text":"Ships a Product Swapper template that pre-wires the whole place-my-product-in-this-scene flow, plus Product In Hand Ad and Product 360 Video Generator for adjacent jobs","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2206","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2205","text":"Magic Resize regenerates a finished image into every ratio you pick, re-composing the frame instead of trimming it","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2208","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2207","text":"Turns one dialed-in SKU into a repeatable process: swap the file on an upload node and everything downstream re-runs on the new product","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2213","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b2210","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2209","text":"Runs every model from ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2211","text":"one subscription","marks":["b2210"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2212","text":" and one credit pool","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2215","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2214","text":"Which model for which job","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b2216","rows":[{"_key":"b2217","cells":[{"_key":"b2218","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2220","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2219","text":"Model","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b2221","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2223","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2222","text":"Best for","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2224","cells":[{"_key":"b2225","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2227","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2226","text":"Nano Banana Pro, by Google","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2228","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2230","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2229","text":"Material, fabric, food, skin tone, editorial lighting","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2231","cells":[{"_key":"b2232","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2234","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2233","text":"GPT Image 2, by OpenAI","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2235","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2237","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2236","text":"Legible type on packaging, labels and on-image copy","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b2238","cells":[{"_key":"b2239","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2241","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2240","text":"Nano Banana 2, by Google","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b2242","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b2244","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2243","text":"Fast exploration before committing to a direction","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2249","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b2246","href":"/blog/nano-banana-image-models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2245","text":"The ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2247","text":"differences between the Nano Banana models","marks":["b2246"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2248","text":" matter more here than they do on a one-off image, because a variant set lives or dies on consistency across the whole batch.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2251","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2250","text":"The qualifier is real setup cost. You're building a graph, and on the first product that's slower than uploading a pack shot to a tool with a single button.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2253","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2252","text":"It pays back on the second SKU. Melius also doesn't publish directly to Meta or TikTok, so if you want creative that goes straight from generation to a live ad set, that handoff stays manual.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2259","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b2256","href":"/pricing","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2254","text":"Best for: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2255","text":"teams producing variants across many SKUs who need the product itself to stay accurate, and who want generating, editing and resizing on one surface. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2257","text":"See pricing","marks":["b2256"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2258","text":" for plans and credits.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2261","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2260","text":"2. Flair","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"2-flair"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2263","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2262","text":"Flair is the closest thing here to a purpose-built e-commerce studio. You stage a scene on a drag-and-drop canvas, position props and your product, then run an AI pass to finish the image, which is a more direct mental model than a node graph if product photography is the only job you have.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2265","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2264","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2267","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2266","text":"Digital scene staging with drag-and-drop props, which makes composition tangible","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2269","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2268","text":"On-model fashion photography that preserves garment patterns","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2271","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2270","text":"A custom AI human model builder for brands that need consistent models","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2273","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2272","text":"Background regeneration and editing tools, plus an API for teams wiring it into a pipeline","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2275","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2274","text":"Flair is narrower by design. It's built around product and on-model imagery, so there's no video, audio or wider content pipeline in the same place, and no agent building the work for you. On staging a product scene it's a fair fight.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2278","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2276","text":"Best for: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2277","text":"e-commerce and fashion teams who want a tool shaped entirely around product and on-model imagery.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2280","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2279","text":"3. Cuttable","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"3-cuttable"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2282","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2281","text":"Cuttable isn't an image tool so much as an ad production system, and that reframing is the point. It learns your brand from your assets and customer research, generates ad variations, then publishes to Meta and TikTok and tracks which ones worked.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2284","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2283","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2286","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2285","text":"Batch ad generation from product imagery and video you already have","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2288","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2287","text":"Brand-trained asset creation that holds visual consistency across a set","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2290","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2289","text":"Direct publishing to Meta and TikTok with automatic resizing","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2292","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2291","text":"Performance data fed back in, so the next batch is informed by the last one","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2294","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2293","text":"Its own framing is that campaign success runs on volume and variation, and it pitches moving a team from five tested ads a week to twenty. That's the right tool if paid social is where your creative lives. It's the wrong one if you need catalog imagery, packaging renders or anything that isn't an ad, and it's aimed at mid-to-large brands with real ad spend rather than a solo operator.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2297","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2295","text":"Best for: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2296","text":"performance marketing teams whose output is paid social creative and who want the publish-and-measure loop closed.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2299","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2298","text":"4. Pencil","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"4-pencil"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2301","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2300","text":"Pencil is built for enterprise teams, and it's honest about that. It describes itself as an AI operating system for marketing teams, pulling models from OpenAI, Google, Adobe, Runway and Bria into one interface with governance wrapped around them.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2303","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2302","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2305","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2304","text":"One editor where you generate, edit and finish an ad without leaving","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2307","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2306","text":"Brand-safe agents coordinating work across 24 markets at once, with role-based access and regional compliance options for the EU, US and APAC","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2309","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2308","text":"Procurement-grade credentials: SOC 2 Type II, IP indemnification, a no-train data policy and granular permissions","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2311","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2310","text":"Named clients including Experian, Diageo, L'Oreal, Japan Airlines and Barilla","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2313","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2312","text":"All of that governance is weight. If you're a five-person brand team, the compliance apparatus is cost without benefit, and enterprise procurement is a months-long motion rather than a signup. Pencil publishes return-on-ad-spend and cost-reduction figures from its own case studies, which are worth reading as vendor claims rather than benchmarks.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2316","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2314","text":"Best for: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2315","text":"large marketing organizations and agencies running multi-market creative where governance and indemnification are purchase requirements.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2318","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2317","text":"5. Creatify","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"5-creatify"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2320","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2319","text":"Creatify is video-first, which makes it the odd one out here in a useful way. Its pitch is AI video ads at the scale your business needs, from ten a month to ten thousand, and it reaches static product imagery through a Product Ads feature that produces studio-quality shots and animations.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2322","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2321","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2324","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2323","text":"URL-to-video, turning a product page straight into a finished ad","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2326","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2325","text":"Batch generation of up to 50 video variants in one run","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2328","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2327","text":"Several entry points into the same job: an agent, an ad flow, a URL, or a blank start","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2330","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2329","text":"Integrations with Meta, TikTok, YouTube, Snap and Amazon","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2332","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2331","text":"If your variant problem is mostly motion, this is the most direct route on the list. If it's mostly stills, you're buying a video platform to do a photo job, and the product-imagery half is a feature rather than the core. User-generated-content-style output is a house strength, which suits some brands and reads wrong for others.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2335","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2333","text":"Best for: ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2334","text":"direct-to-consumer teams whose testing budget goes into short-form video and who want static product shots from the same tool.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2337","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2336","text":"What a variant set actually costs you","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-a-variant-set-actually-costs-you"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2339","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2338","text":"The per-image price is the least interesting number in this comparison. What actually costs money is the second pass.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2341","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2340","text":"Work it through on one SKU. You need a hero shot, three lifestyle scenes, and each of those at three aspect ratios, which is twelve assets.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2343","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2342","text":"Generating them is minutes. What eats the afternoon is the near-misses: the shot where the product sits at the wrong scale, the resize that pushed your logo off-canvas, the label that came back unreadable.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2345","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2344","text":"So the question to ask a tool in a trial isn't how good is the first image. It's how cheap is the correction. On a canvas you edit the node's prompt and re-run that step.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2347","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2346","text":"In a one-shot generator you start the brief again. Across twelve assets and a few dozen SKUs, that difference dwarfs any per-image rate, which is also why a cheaper generator and a pricier one often land in the same place once the corrections are counted.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2349","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2348","text":"Producing variants on Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"producing-variants-on-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2351","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2350","text":"Start with the three inputs, not the prompt. A clean pack shot on a file node, the product page URL pasted into the chat so Mel scrapes the real dimensions and materials into a text node, and your logo as its own node with an instruction not to redraw it. Then generate three or four variations at a time and correct the near-misses by editing that step's prompt.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2359","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b2353","href":"/blog/best-ai-photo-background-editing-tools","isNewTab":false},{"_type":"link","_key":"b2356","href":"/blog/connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2352","text":"Once one image is right, Magic Resize produces each channel ratio by re-composing the frame rather than trimming it, and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2354","text":"background work stays on the same canvas","marks":["b2353"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2355","text":" if a scene needs replacing. To run the whole sequence without clicking through it, ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2357","text":"an agent can drive the canvas over MCP","marks":["b2356"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2358","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2364","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b2361","href":"/blog/ai-brand-mockup-tools-ranked","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2360","text":"If the brief is a branded scene rather than a product shot, the same compositing approach carries over, covered in ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2362","text":"AI brand mockup tools, ranked","marks":["b2361"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2363","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2369","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b2366","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2365","text":"Try it on one real SKU: drop in a pack shot, paste the product page URL, and see how far the fidelity holds. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2367","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b2366"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b2368","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b2371","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b2370","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b2372","items":"$4e:props:children:1:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:post:faq"}]}}],"$L62","$L63"]}]]}]]}]
